    "q-132492": {
      "dom_id": "step-q132492",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X∼B(50,0.58),$ use the normal approximation to the binomial distribution to approximate $P(25\\le X\\le 30).$ Give your final answer to three decimal places.\n\n*Hint: The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.08\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.09\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.3\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0854\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0838\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0823\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.2\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1020\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1003\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0985\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.1\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1210\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1190\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1170\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.02\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.03\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.04\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.4\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6628\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6664\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6700\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.5\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6985\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.7019\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.7054\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.6\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.7324\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.7357\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.7389\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "Given a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ if \n\n- $np>5,$ and\n\n- $n(1-p)>5,$\n\nwe can approximate $X$ as a normal random variable $Y$ with mean $\\mu =np$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=np(1-p),$ that is, \n\n$$\nY∼N(np,np(1-p)).\n$$\n\nHere, we have $n=50$ and $p=0.58.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}np & =50\\cdot 0.58 \\\\  & =29 \\\\  & >5\\,✓ \\\\ n(1-p) & =50\\cdot (1-0.58) \\\\  & =21 \\\\  & >5.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can approximate our binomial random variable $X$ with a normal random variable $Y$ with mean\n\n$$\n\\mu =np=(50)(0.58)=29\n$$\n\nand variance\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=np(1-p)=(50)(0.58)(1-0.58)=12.18.\n$$\n\nThat is, we can approximate $X$ by $Y∼N(29,12.18).$\n\nNow, we can estimate the desired probability $P(25\\le X\\le 30).$ Using a continuity correction, we have\n\n$$\nP(25\\le X\\le 30)≈P(24.5\\le Y\\le 30.5).\n$$\n\nTo compute this probability, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(24.5\\le Y\\le 30.5) & =P(\\frac{24.5-29}{\\sqrt{12.18}}\\le Z\\le \\frac{30.5-29}{\\sqrt{12.18}}) \\\\  & ≈P(-1.29\\le Z\\le 0.43) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.43)-P(Z<-1.29) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.43)-P(Z\\le -1.29) \\\\  & =Φ(0.43)-Φ(-1.29) \\\\  & =0.6664-0.0985 \\\\  & =0.5679\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(25\\le X\\le 30)≈0.568.\n$$\n\nNote: Using a software package for the approximation gives a probability of $0.5646.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
